      "title": "epan: Fix elastic-mapping types",
      "message": "epan: Fix elastic-mapping types\n\n\"byte\" means an 8-bit signed integer FT_INT8, not FT_BYTES.\n\nThere's now an unsigned long type for FT_UINT64.\n\nFT_INT16 fits in a \"short\".\n\nAdd the rarely-used FT_INT40 and FT_INT56.\n\nFT_DOUBLE needs a double, and FT_RELATIVE_DATE isn't a \"date\"\n(which is for absolute dates - any times since the epoch should\nbe FT_ABSOLUTE_DATE) but also needs a double (or possibly a\n\"scaled_float\" with a 10^9 scaling factor to preserve precision.)\n\nFor FT_ABSOLUTE_DATE, all supported versions of ElasticSearch/OpenSearch\nsupport \"date_nanos\" (it internally uses a 64-bit integer of nanoseconds,\nwhich creates a Y2262 problem, but that should be ok with our actual data.)\n\nPing #19657\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
